       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. The dose is 5,100 mg per day, double the maximum labeled dose, and a non-prescriber can't authorize it. I can't tell whether it's intentional or an error, and if it's an error the patient could be seriously harmed.\n\nThese are the ways to move forward:\n- **The prescribing clinician enters the order.** They can enter it directly or tell me the dose they want. If they intend an above-maximum dose, they should document the rationale. Pharmacy will probably need to verify it.\n- **I enter a standard dose.** If you or the clinician give me a dose within the labeled range, such as 850 mg three times daily with meals, I'll enter it right away.\n- **Pharmacy or the medicine service attending reviews it.** They can check what the patient actually needs.\n\nJust tell me which dose you'd like."
